    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n20634" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Hĭbernĭa</span></b> , ae,
			f. (= <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἰουερνία</span> Ptol.),
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>the island now
				called Ireland</i>, <i><span class="en">Caes. B. G. 5, 13, 2</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Plin. 4, 16,
				30, § 103</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Tac. Agr. 24</span></i>.— Also
			called <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Iverna</span></b> ,
			ae, <i><span class="en">Mel. 3, 6, 6</span></i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Ju-verna</span></b> , ae, <i><span class="en">Juv. 2,
			160</span></i>; and (acc. to the Gr. form <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἰέρνη</span> Strab.) <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Ierna</span></b> , ae, App. de Mundo, p. 60; and <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Iernē</span></b> ,
				ēs, <i><span class="en">Claud. Laud.
				Stil. 2, 251</span></i>; IV. Cons. Hon. 33.</div>
